erioration; provides for the orderly use, improvement and development of such lands; and provides for the stabilization of the livestock industry dependent upon","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-app-executive-orders-6910-407c8cb464.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"7d52335dcf4c574b3a81dbcfad2a359865b1ec991bd7146baf0f2ec656004e8f","source":{"line":2265,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"0c0dced964a20dfd1c5a787dd5e869b837fed204e124160f540545f6b9426138"}},{"first_1500_characters":"{\"member\": \"usc02.xml\", \"note_id\": \"iddcb8117d-3a6e-11f1-a0f3-db3efcbbb4ee\", \"citation\": \"2 U.S.C. 685 note\", \"heading\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\", \"subjects\": [\"11845\"], \"status_line\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\", \"t","path":"jobs/current-law/output/USC_EO_NOTES.jsonl","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"ac1e287b6b606b8adc5c1975f662aae2d31989c1d072e32c89dbc38f6efe8016","source":{"line":3,"path":"jobs/current-law/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"5b6e5de61be4ea9c9c4749827c02d0c9d484107505b7e9adae3172a42351c188"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 2300.0-3 Authority.\n(a)(1) Section 204 of the Federal Land Policy and Management Act of 1976 (43 U.S.C. 1714) gives the Secretary of the Interior general authority to make, modify, extend or revoke withdrawals, but only in accordance with the provisions and limitations of that section. Among other limitations, the Federal Land Policy and Management Act of 1976 provides that the Secretary of the ","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t43-2300.0-3.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"33342f1e72c6e9200c2cd7701bcc029dddf59fbff1bcf1b88ffeb23fb43cbd5a","source":{"line":421,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"19fa6baf254c43782fd8d3fcaeb1f49938f0e50702ed97af9305ddd5d13bd55c"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 2400.0-3 Authority.\n(a) All vacant public lands, except those in Alaska, have been, with certain exceptions, withdrawn from entry, selection, and location under the nonmineral land laws by Executive Order 6910, of November 26, 1934, and Executive Order 6964 of February 5, 1935, and amendments thereto, and by the establishment of grazing districts under section 1 of the Act of June 28, 1934 (48 S","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t43-2400.0-3.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"62f15873bc34537b6d276e42b6388f2b7852e33f57d9e00739155ee6ff73f9c4","source":{"line":422,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"adcfa709956b723b40ccd8c12da793e1a425ba7cd9a90981fdb169b1b75f30a1"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 2520.0-8 Land subject to disposition.\n(a) Land that may be entered as desert land. (1) As the desert-land law requires the artificial irrigation of any land entered thereunder, lands which are not susceptible of irrigation by practicable means are not deemed subject to entry as desert lands. The question as to whether any particular tract sought to be entered as desert land is in fact irrigable ","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t43-2520.0-8.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"ce652e4cddfc630c1bfff1dd011dfcfe97677e7b597bac8e8e20513b72514d24","source":{"line":423,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"77761a4e0fd8bc1bb3c26c72add004486f137587c685ed88750b22fdef39ed3f"}}]}
